# ── WhatsApp session state — NEVER COMMIT ───────────────────────────────────
#
# These directories hold Baileys authentication state: device identity, Signal
# identity keys, pre-keys and app-state sync keys. That is FULL ACCESS to the
# linked WhatsApp account. A commit here is an account compromise, and one that
# survives in git history after the file is deleted.
#
# Listed first, and deliberately broad, because the cost of a false positive
# (an ignored file you meant to track) is trivial next to the alternative.
data/
sessions/
*.session
creds.json
*creds*.json
app-state-sync-key-*.json
pre-key-*.json
sender-key-*.json
session-*.json

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Logs / coverage / scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
.nyc_output/
tmp/
.DS_Store
